---
code: transport-not-attempted
when-fires: no session process could be created, so the host was never contacted. cli/transport_edge.rs. {host} is the destination that went uncontacted, {detail} the spawn failure.
why: AID-NEEDS:law-codes-vary-by-world-not-grammar. The one transport outcome licensed to claim the host was untouched, because the failure is local and provable - the controller could not spawn a child at all. Every other no-output case cannot separate never-ran from ran-and-was-lost.
